-- title:
--   Unique centre place of a crossing-presented node
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$ and a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$. Let $k_0/\mathbb Q$ be a subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ an element lying in $A$, such that $A_0:=A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal $(\pi_0)$, is henselian, has algebraically closed residue field, and such that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo $\mathfrak m_A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$. Give $\bar F:=$ `fieldBar q M'`, an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\overline{\mathbb Q}$ attached to the level $q^2M'$ full-level function field, its induced $k_0$-algebra structure. Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $k_0\subseteq\bar F$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot F_0=\bar F$ and linearly disjoint from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over finite layers, in the sense that for every finite extension $K'/k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, any finite family of elements of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ that is $K'$-linearly independent admits no non-trivial vanishing linear combination with coefficients in $K'\cdot F_0$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $F_0$ which is a discrete valuation ring, agrees with $A$ on $k_0$ (for $x\in k_0$, $x\in A$ iff its image lies in $W_0$), and has maximal ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$. Let $\mathcal O\subseteq W_0$ be a noetherian local subring of $F_0$ which again agrees with $A$ on $k_0$, whose residue field is exhausted by the constants (every $f\in\mathcal O$ differs from the image of some $x\in k_0\cap A$ by a non-unit of $\mathcal O$), and whose fraction field is $F_0$ (every $f\in F_0$ is $g/h$ with $g,h\in\mathcal O$, $h\ne 0$). Assume a crossing presentation: an integer $E_0\ge 1$, elements $c_x,c_y\in\mathcal O$, a unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$ with $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$, and a ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal O$ at its maximal ideal onto the crossing model $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2,\widehat{A_0})/\mathrm{uvCrossingIdeal}$ at $\pi_0^{E_0}$ over the adic completion $\widehat{A_0}$, such that $\iota$ carries constants from $k_0\cap A$ to the corresponding constant series, and $\iota(c_x)=\gamma_U\,U$, $\iota(c_y)=\gamma_V\,V$ for units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of the crossing model; assume moreover $c_y\in\mathfrak m_{W_0}$ and $c_x\in W_0\setminus\mathfrak m_{W_0}$. Finally let $FSS$ be a field over the residue field of $A$ and let $R$ be a regular prolongation of $A$ to $\bar F$ with residue field target $FSS$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $\bar F$ meeting $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in $A$, together with a surjective residue map to $FSS$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal and which extends reduction on $A$), and assume $R.\mathrm{integers}\cap F_0=W_0$. Then there is a place $nd$ of $FSS$ over the residue field of $A$ — a proper valuation subring of $FSS$ containing the image of $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ and a principal ideal ring — which is rational (the residue field of $nd$ is generated by $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$), such that the reduction $R.\mathrm{residue}$ maps $\mathcal O$ into the valuation subring of $nd$ and maps the non-units of $\mathcal O$ into its maximal ideal; $nd$ is the unique place of $FSS$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ with these two properties; the reduction of $c_y$ is $0$; and the reduction of $c_x$ has $nd$-order equal to $1$, where the order is minus the logarithm of the associated discrete adic valuation.
--
--   This is the node-point statement for the semistable model of the full-level modular curve: a node presented by a crossing $UV=\pi_0^{E_0}$ determines a unique rational centre place on the reduced function field, at which the vertical coordinate $c_y$ vanishes and the transverse coordinate $c_x$ becomes a uniformiser. It feeds the per-node analysis of layered node rings and node charts, namely [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_nodeCentre_igusaEnd_layeredNodeRings_of_mem_nodes_igusaSep_layerExponent`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_nodeCentre_igusaEnd_layeredNodeRings_of_mem_nodes_igusaSep_layerExponent) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodeCore_nodeCharts_hasseGerm_nodeCentre_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodeCore_nodeCharts_hasseGerm_nodeCentre_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep).
